 # Projective Spatial Transformer (ProST)
-
-
 ## Overview
 ProST is a differentiable volume rendering module that generalizes spatial transformers to projective geometry, enabling volumetric rendering of transmission images that are differentiable with respect to both the input volume and the pose parameters [S1]. It solves the problem of performing end-to-end differentiable projection of voxelized data onto 2D planes, which is essential for tasks like 2D/3D registration where gradients must flow from a 2D similarity metric back through the projection to the 3D pose [S1]. Unlike mesh-based differentiable renderers, ProST operates directly on voxel grids using a cone-beam ray casting approach, making it suitable for medical imaging applications [S1].
